resolution: pm lint renders TOON and global --json through the host with repeatable flags and verdict exit codes
expected_result: Packed npm and Bun consumers exit 0 clean and 1 on configured findings
actual_result: "CI test (22), test (26) and codeql green on PR #6; orchestrator-run isolated npm release:check 78/78 with 100% coverage; orchestrator packed install: TOON and JSON output, real flag descriptions in --help"
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-12T14:16:51.878Z",codex-sol,Host registration exposes repeatable rule disable and id flags. Scalar validation rejects malformed flags. SDK testing activation and real temporary trackers exercise the native command dispatcher; packed acceptance verifies TOON JSON and process exit behavior.
  "2026-10-12T14:28:10.100Z",pi-glm-tooling,"Packed-consumer acceptance (pm package install of the built tarball into npm and Bun consumers) surfaced three real-host contract gaps in the lint command registration; precise diagnosis and fixes are recorded under follow-up task pm-lint-1c6j: manifest schema capability, FlagDefinition.long without the value placeholder (list/value_name for repeatables), and omitting exit_code 0 from the command result. test/install.acceptance.ts encodes these contracts and will pass once they land."
  "2026-10-12T14:28:45.699Z",codex-sol,"SDK authoring gaps: registered flags need separate long names and value_name; long strings containing value placeholders can appear in help yet be rejected during invocation. Typed flags require manifest schema capability. Explicit handler exit_code 0 is rejected; the adapter uses SDK printResult and suppressHostOutput, with host exit control only for nonzero verdicts. Rendered receipts still carry exit_code 0 or 1."
